      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> STAT_U03_L06_Q09</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.STAT.BVM.7</p><div class='assessment-visual'><p><strong>Two-way table:</strong></p><table border='1' cellpadding='5' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0;'><tr><th>Grade / Preference</th><th>Online notes</th><th>Printed notes</th><th>Row total</th></tr><tr><td>Grade 9</td><td>18</td><td>12</td><td>30</td></tr><tr><td>Grade 10</td><td>22</td><td>38</td><td>60</td></tr><tr><td>Column total</td><td>40</td><td>50</td><td>90</td></tr></table><p>Inside cells are joint frequencies. Row and column totals are marginal frequencies. The grand total is 90.</p></div><p>What is the grand total in a two-way table?</p>]]></text>
